QcomDwc3 (unixnu-research/QcomDwc3, main e4efe95c903a737e0f5955e5b50a8fb4d2a7d718; BSD-2-Clause-Patent except QcomEusb2Phy.h and
QcomQmpUsb3.h, which are GPL-2.0-only and were not read for this), facts and design only, no code: QcomDwc3.cpp (sha256
4b29c0aa6ed893c9b11b1c129795a2c1ddd9bf44e39ad79e2294de61113250f2) runs Apple's AppleUSBXHCI on SM8550 behind a hand-made nub (an
IODeviceMemory of 0x8000 bytes at the core, name usb-host0, a bus-number property, the interrupt over armcpu_spi_attach), with a core
soft reset and GCTL.PRTCAPDIR between the roles and the roles from UCSI; QcomUcsi.h (sha256
5c688feeddd335ddc3e2f06baa9909fc7fbd1712285b6216d23bb85a60cf94b3) is the UCSI client a later level derives from
(docs/drivers/usb-host.md sections 4 and 9).

Project-SunUEFI (unixnu-research/Project-SunUEFI, main 4ef87402e9d58465af871e4c4f4a5de87599d81c), BSD-2-Clause-Patent, facts only:
docs/archive/storage-usb/usb-host-port-plan.md (sha256 8f6e2f6b57d3f9cd9b1adb1edc8d25daaa6610a908a904bac438ab40550df512) and
docs/devel/boot/uefi-console.md (sha256 cf929a24a8053ec04d5a924e176d6a717ff7057b084b49d9ff3f32de4a92d193): the xHCI window
(0xa600000, 32 KiB), the hi-lo 64-bit write order of the DWC3 xHCI, the Type-C block's MODE_CFG reading 0x02 (sink only) when UEFI
starts, the repeater's host tuning overrides, DP_COM TYPEC_CTRL at 0x088e8010, no VBUS control in the stock UEFI.

